WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.367
-Our next guest is
an award-winning chef

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.501
and founder of
Milk Bar Bakeries.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:05.634
She's one of our favorites.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:06.868
She has a new book out called

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.901
"Dessert Can Save the World."

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:12.100
Please welcome Chef Christina
Tosi, ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Come on, now!

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:17.868
Welcome back. We love you.
Welcome, welcome back.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:20.033
This is your first memoir.
-It is.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.400
I just felt like it was
an important message

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.167
when I was writing it,
and it continues to remind me

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.968
now that it's out that
it's like a rally call.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:31.033
It's a reminder that we need
joy, that joy matters,

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:34.634
that knowing ourselves, finding
these moments that connect us

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.834
to ourselves, to other people,
to the world,

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.634
these are like the connective
tissues that make life worth

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:43.767
living and fighting for and like
just being good and doing good.

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.067
That's what the book's
all about.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.701
-There's little things in here
that make me laugh.

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:48.534
There's things called
"dirty dessert secrets."

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.100
-Mm-hmm.
-Can you explain what those are?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.234
-Yes, I can.
-Thank you.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:53.100
-The things, for me,
my dirty dessert secrets

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.634
are all like pantry-loading,
right?

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.434
Like, it's late at night,
no one's home.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.434
I had a day, I need a moment.

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:01.868
So I brought for you some of my
favorite dirty dessert secrets.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:04.834
I have hot cocoa mix
and maple syrup.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.501
You mix it until it becomes like
a fudgy consistency.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.601
Get in there.
I'm gonna spoon some for Quest.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:11.033
You can just have
a little nibble.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:12.834
Look at this. Also, I forgot
to tell you number-one rule of

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.601
dirty dessert secrets --
no judgment.

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:16.100
-Okay.
-This is a judgment-free zone.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.200
-But this is maple syrup
and hot cocoa mix.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.734
Wow.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.367
-You're not mad at it, are you?

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.901
-How'd you do that?
-You're not mad at it.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.567
-I'm not mad at all.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.501
You ready for the next one?
-I love that. Yes.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.801
-M&amp;Ms.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.334
You pour hot water over them.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.934
You strain them out like this.
-Whoa!

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:37.267
-Very, very strange color.

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.167
You mash them around
with a spoon

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:40.400
and then you eat them.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.734
Take a little spoonful.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.801
-It's fantastic.
-Oh, yo!

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.133
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, right?

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.334
This is it.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:47.667
Okay, you ready for this one?

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.834
For me, it, like, brings me
back to high school days.

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:51.033
You take a honey bun.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.701
You warm it up in the microwave.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.200
You mash it down.
-This is one I read in the book.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.801
-You put a Snickers in it.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:56.634
You roll it up.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:57.667
Get in there, guys.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.200
-So, it's a honey bun --

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.501
-Wrapped around a Snickers.
-Wrapped around a Snickers bar.

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.300
-Microwaved.
-And microwaved.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.167
Alright, I'm taking this.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.901
-Tell me. Talk to me.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:11.067
You mad at it?
-How do you think of this?

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.934
-This is, like --

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.801
-That is -- That's the winner.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.434
-That's the win-- You aren't
even there yet, though.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:18.467
-That's the winner right there.
-Okay, you ready for this?

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.601
This, for me, is like
church days a little bit.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:23.567
It's a piece of white bread,
some margarine, and some Tang.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.701
It's called Tang Toast.
-[ Laughs ] Wait, what?

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:28.267
-It's called Tang Toast.

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:29.767
Get in there.
I'm coming right behind you

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:31.200
'cause my next one is coming up.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.667
-Fairy bread.
-Yeah.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.801
-Is your soul feeling lit up
right now?

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.601
-Yes, it is. It's from
the honey bun Snickers.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:39.234
-You first.

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.834
-Oh, wow.
-Are you mixing Mountain Dew?

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:45.334
-I'm mixing cake mix
and a can of Mountain Dew.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:48.067
And then it gets microwaved
5, 10 seconds.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.033
Just go with me. Open mind.

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.334
I hear you over there.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.167
Yo, this has been my move.

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.033
I'm not kidding.
I had it without Mountain Dew

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.767
but with peanut butter and milk
the other night.

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:59.868
This is my always
dirty dessert secret go-to.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.434
You ready for this?

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.834
It's a little warm.
It's a little gooey.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.667
Judgment-free zone, guys.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:06.834
Get in there.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:07.968
-Mountain Dew --
-His face right now.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:10.000
-Yeah, yeah. Get in there.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.501
-Mountain Dew and cake mix.

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.267
-Your life is
going to be changed.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:19.367
-Wow.

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.767
-This is just -- This is what
Milk Bar was built on, guys.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.534
-How did you think of this?
-How did you think of this?

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.367
-No way, the best one
is yet to come.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.067
But this is a real trust fall,
okay?

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.834
-Okay.
-Judgment-free zone.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.934
It's not about how we portray
ourselves to the outside world.

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:34.634
It's about what happens
when no one's looking.

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.100
-Just do it.
-You ready for this?

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.534
You guys got to close your eyes.

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.868
I got you --
I got you some masks.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.901
Quest, that's for you.
-I don't know.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:43.868
-Jims, this is for you.
-I don't know anything about it.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.434
-Okay.
-Just trust me. Trust me.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.634
-We always do.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.968
-Yeah. I believe in you guys.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.467
Okay.
-Can you see anything?

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:54.734
-I'm going to give you something
and each of you just pinch this.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.734
Yep. Just hold it like that.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:58.601
I'm going to give you something
to dunk it in.

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:00.701
Okay, there we go.

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:03.167
No peeking yet. No peeking yet.

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.367
[ Audience ohs ]
-Wait, why's the audience --

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.033
-I know. The audience is ewwing.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:08.701
-It's 'cause they're jealous.
It's 'cause they're jealous.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:09.968
Okay, give me a dunk.

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:12.100
Dunk but dunk like a big dunk.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.367
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
No, no, not yet, Jimmy.

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:15.767
-Like this?
-Is that your arm?

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:18.968
-That's my arm. Okay, hold on.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:20.934
-Love your perfume.
-Can I dunk it?

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:22.133
A big dunk. You got it,

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:24.400
but no, come back in,
a bigger dunk, Jimmy.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.467
Okay.
-Yeah.

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:26.901
-Did I dunk it?

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:28.167
Get in there, one, two, three.
-So consume this?

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.567
-Bottoms up. Consume.

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:34.767
Do it, do it.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:36.734
Okay, you want to know
what you just had?

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.234
Okay. Masks off, guys.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.267
Flaming hot Cheetos,
vanilla frosting.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.400
This is the ultimate
dirty dessert secret.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.133
-Yeah, I dig it, too.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:46.167
-You are a genius. How do you
come up with this stuff?

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:48.334
We love you.
Christina Tosi, everyone.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:50.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:54.634
"Dessert Can Save the World"
is out now.

